Hi,

Im not sure how many NaNs you get in the gc content you calculate. If it is a significant proportion, something can be wrong. Are the coordinates in your bed file in concordance with the hg38 human reference?

If the input is correct, you can proceed as below:

After gc = getgc(…), you can use the code below to set all NaN and NA to 0 , which will be futher removed in the QC step.

gc[is.na <http://is.na>(gc)]=0

gc[is.nan(gc)]=0

